# DTF tier manifest: rolling-deploy-migrations  (artifact-keeper#5920, 1.13.0)
# Profile-set: filesystem + migrations.ignore-missing.
#
# THE PROBLEM (#5920)
# In a rolling update the new pods apply their migrations as they start, so
# the previous release serves on the newer schema until the rollout ends. A
# pod of the previous release that restarts in that window (OOM, node drain)
# finds versions in _sqlx_migrations it does not embed, and sqlx fails with
# VersionMissing: the pod crash-loops until the rollout finishes, and for good
# if the rollout is paused or rolled back.
#
# THE FIX (1.13.0)
# MIGRATIONS_IGNORE_MISSING=true: the backend starts on a newer ledger when
# every newer migration is an expand, or a contract of an expand it embeds
# (description `contract of MMM ...`, from a NNN_contract_of_MMM_<what>.sql
# file the expand/contract CI check requires). It refuses a newer contract
# of an expand it does not have.
#
# THE PRIMITIVE: THE NEXT RELEASE'S EXPAND MIGRATION, SIMULATED
# The oracle plays release N+1 against this slot's own Postgres: it adds a
# nullable column to `repositories` (an expand) and records it in
# _sqlx_migrations under a version far above the binary's, with a plain
# description. It then restarts the backend container, which is "release N
# restarting mid-rollout".
#
# Oracle (discriminating, RELEASE_GATE=1):
#   (CONTROL) before: /readyz 200, a public download 200.
#   (FIX #5920) after the restart on the newer expand-only ledger the backend
#             serves: /readyz 200 within 120 s, the download 200 + bytes, and
#             an upload 201 on the expanded table. RED on main: the container
#             exits with VersionMissing.
#   (FIX #5920) with a newer `contract of <the binary's newest migration>`
#             recorded too, the restarted backend serves: it is past that
#             expand. RED on main: VersionMissing.
#   (CONTROL) with a newer `contract of <the simulated expand>` recorded as
#             well, the restarted backend never serves (both images exit).
#   (FIX #5920) the refusal names that contract migration. RED on main: only
#             VersionMissing.
#   (CONTROL) with the simulated rows and column removed, the backend
#             restarts and serves again.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem migrations.ignore-missing"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
COVERS="5920"
export MIGRATIONS_IGNORE_MISSING="true"
